# What you see while stopped. Set a breakpoint on the "yield", then open each
# scope in the Variables panel:
# - Registers: r15 (Stage), and r1 labelled with the vent it holds the ID of.
# - Stack: 0, then "1 (top)" at sp, then "10 (above sp)", which put wrote.
# - Devices: d0 vent, d1 sensor, db, then pa on the network. pa's gas
#   readings come from the pipe, so they can't be edited.
# - Atmospheres (the pipe, the outside air), World (tick, lines this tick),
#   Defines.
# Inline values: while stopped, each line up to the one stopped at shows its
# registers, aliases and device properties at its end (Stage = 2, Vent.On = 1),
# and the entry a put or get addresses (stack[10] = 3). Stop on a push to see
# where it writes and what it would overwrite, or on the peek to see what it reads.
# Things to try:
# - Double-click r15 (Stage) and type Max. Double-click the vent's On and type 0.
# - Hover Stage, then Setting (a logic type: its description).
# - Add vent.On to Watch.
# - Type coolant or d0.On in the Debug Console.
alias Stage r15
alias Vent d0
alias Sensor d1
define Max 5
define Warm 300
move Stage 1
l r1 Vent ReferenceId
push 7
push 8
put db 10 3
loop:
l r2 Sensor Temperature
sgt r3 r2 Warm
s Vent On r3
add Stage Stage 1
peek r4 # the top of the stack: 8
get r5 db 10 # what the put wrote: 3
add r6 r4 r5
s db Setting r6
yield
j loop
